<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />

    <title>
      <% if (!project) { %>
        Project Not Found | Alex Draesner
      <% } else if (project.slug === 'web-development') { %>
        AlexBlog | Alex Draesner
      <% } else { %>
        <%= project.name %> | Alex Draesner
      <% } %>
    </title>

    <link href="/css/style.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  </head>

  <body class="project-detail-body">
    <header class="site-header">
      <a class="site-logo" href="/">Alex Draesner</a>

      <nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Main navigation">
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/home">Overview</a></li>
          <li><a href="/about">About Me</a></li>
          <li><a class="active" href="/projects">Projects</a></li>
        </ul>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main class="project-detail-page">
      <% if (!project) { %>
        <section class="project-not-found">
          <p class="project-eyebrow">Project unavailable</p>

          <h1>Project not found</h1>

          <p>
            This project may have been removed or the link may be incorrect.
          </p>

          <a class="project-button" href="/projects">
            Back to projects
          </a>
        </section>
      <% } else { %>
        <% const description = project.description || '' %>
        <% const notionMatch = description.match(/(https?:\/\/\S+)/) %>
        <% const cleanDescription = notionMatch
          ? description.replace(notionMatch[1], '').trim()
          : description %>

        <% let projectImage = project.image || null %>

        <% if (project.slug === '3d-printing') {
          projectImage = '/3d-pager.png'
        } else if (project.slug === 'web-development') {
          projectImage = '/alex-blog.png'
        } %>

        <% const displayName = project.slug === 'web-development'
          ? 'AlexBlog'
          : project.name %>

        <a class="back-link" href="/projects">
          ← Back to projects
        </a>

        <section class="project-detail-hero">
          <p class="project-eyebrow">Selected project</p>

          <h1><%= displayName %></h1>

          <% if (project.slug === '3d-printing') { %>
            <p class="project-lead">
              Exploring 3D design, physical prototyping, and iterative making
              through a pager-inspired university project.
            </p>
          <% } else if (project.slug === 'web-development') { %>
            <p class="project-lead">
              A private full-stack blog project built to practise frontend
              development, backend routing, templating, and user-focused
              interface design.
            </p>
          <% } else { %>
            <p class="project-lead">
              Explore the process, tools, and learning behind this project.
            </p>
          <% } %>
        </section>

        <section class="project-detail-layout">
          <figure class="project-image-card">
            <% if (projectImage) { %>
              <img
                src="<%= projectImage %>"
                alt="<%= displayName %> project preview"
              />
            <% } else { %>
              <div class="project-image-placeholder">
                <span><%= displayName %></span>
              </div>
            <% } %>

            <figcaption>
              <%= displayName %>
            </figcaption>
          </figure>

          <article class="project-description-card">
            <p class="project-card-label">Project overview</p>

            <% if (project.slug === '3d-printing') { %>
              <h2>From digital model to physical prototype</h2>

              <p>
                For my first university project, InsightOut, our team designed
                pager-like devices inspired by Digimon.
              </p>

              <p>
                I created the 3D models in my modelling application and
                handled most of the printing. We developed and printed multiple
                versions while refining the shape and design of the device.
              </p>

              <h3>My contribution</h3>

              <ul class="project-detail-list">
                <li>Created the 3D models for the pager-like device</li>
                <li>Prepared and produced most of the printed parts</li>
                <li>Iterated on the design through multiple versions</li>
                <li>Helped turn a digital concept into a physical prototype</li>
              </ul>

              <div class="project-tags">
                <span>3D design</span>
                <span>3D printing</span>
                <span>Prototyping</span>
                <span>Iteration</span>
              </div>

              <% if (notionMatch) { %>
                <a
                  class="project-button"
                  href="<%= notionMatch[1].trim() %>"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                >
                  View the project gallery →
                </a>
              <% } %>

            <% } else if (project.slug === 'web-development') { %>
              <h2>Building a private full-stack blog</h2>

              <p>
                AlexBlog is a private blog project built with Node.js, Express,
                EJS, HTML, and CSS. I created it to practise building a
                server-rendered website with multiple pages and user-focused
                content.
              </p>

              <p>
                The project includes blog post pages, a contact form, Express
                routes, EJS templates, and a themed interface. It is not
                currently deployed publicly, so the image shows a local version
                of the website.
              </p>

              <h3>What I practised</h3>

              <ul class="project-detail-list">
                <li>Creating routes with Node.js and Express</li>
                <li>Rendering pages with EJS templates</li>
                <li>Structuring pages with HTML and styling them with CSS</li>
                <li>Building blog post and contact-page functionality</li>
                <li>Organising a multi-page web application</li>
              </ul>

              <div class="project-tags">
                <span>HTML</span>
                <span>CSS</span>
                <span>JavaScript</span>
                <span>Node.js</span>
                <span>Express</span>
                <span>EJS</span>
              </div>

            <% } else { %>
              <h2>Project overview</h2>

              <p>
                <%= cleanDescription || 'Project details coming soon.' %>
              </p>

              <% if (notionMatch) { %>
                <a
                  class="project-button"
                  href="<%= notionMatch[1].trim() %>"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                >
                  View more details →
                </a>
              <% } %>
            <% } %>
          </article>
        </section>
      <% } %>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>